# git worktrees created for isolated task branches (e.g. `git worktree add
# .worktrees/<branch>`) are machine-local checkouts of history already in
# .git, not site content.
.worktrees/

# ── machine-local, not part of the site ──────────────────────────────────
# There is no package.json here and there must never be one (see CLAUDE.md),
# so a lockfile can only be the residue of a stray `npm install` or of running
# tools/make-icons.mjs. Ignored rather than committed, because committing it
# would be the first half of exactly the version carrier this repo refuses to
# grow.
package-lock.json
node_modules/

# read/config.js is DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED. read/index.html loads it with a
# <script src>, so a missing file is a 404 in every reader's console on every
# page load.
#
# 2026-09-07: it now carries a real apiUrl, and this paragraph used to say it
# would not. The old plan was an empty committed copy that "a deploy overwrites
# with the real per-deployment values" -- but this site is GitHub Pages served
# STRAIGHT FROM THE BRANCH, with no .github/workflows and no deploy step of any
# kind to do that overwriting. An empty committed copy therefore meant sharing
# was permanently off, not "configured later".
#
# What did NOT change is that this repo holds no secret. publishableKey stays
# EMPTY: mak-share is deployed with verify_jwt off, and a POST carrying no
# apikey and no Authorization header was measured answering 200, so read.js's
# `if (CONFIG.publishableKey)` simply sends neither header. The apiUrl is not a
# secret either -- it is the address in every request the reader's own browser
# makes, and read.js refuses any origin outside ALLOWED_API_ORIGINS regardless.

# Redesign mockup preview — not part of the published site.
preview/
